As the ocean's waves crashed onto the shore,
A symphony of sound, a dance of the tide;
The sand, a canvas, waiting to be told,
A story of the sea, in patterns bold.

The waves swept up, a swirling vortex,
A whirlpool of water, a maelstrom of might;
The sand, a sifter, separating the fine,
From the coarse, the pebbles, the shells that shine.

As the tide pulled back, the patterns remained,
A poem of the ocean, a tale of the deep;
A language of the waves, a dialect of the sea,
A message from the depths, for all to see.

The poem told of secrets, of mysteries untold;
Of the creatures that lurk, in the dark below;
Of the sunken ships, of the treasures that lie;
Of the ocean's power, and its beauty that never dies.

The poem spoke of the cycles, of the ebb and flow;
Of the tides that rise, and the tides that go;
Of the constant change, of the eternal sea;
A reminder of the power, that lies beneath the surface, you see.

The poem ended, the patterns faded away;
But the memory of the sea, remained, come what may;
A symbol of the unknown, a mystery to unfold;
A reminder of the beauty, that lies beneath the waves, so cold.

